              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - CVE-2026-0540 Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:javascript\/DOMPurify@3.1.6"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "DOMPurify 3.1.3 through 3.3.1 and 2.5.3 through 2.5.8, fixed in commit 2726c74, contain a cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows attackers to bypass attribute sanitization by exploiting five missing rawtext elements (noscript, xmp, noembed, noframes, iframe) in the SAFE_FOR_XML regex. Attackers can include payloads like <\/noscript><img src=x onerror=alert(1)> in attribute values to execute JavaScript when sanitized output is placed inside these unprotected rawtext contexts."
