          "ruleId": "CVE-2026-41239",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-41239 - DOMPurify's SAFE_FOR_TEMPLATES feature fails to strip Mustache\/template expressions when RETURN_DOM or RETURN_DOM_FRAGMENT is used. The final string-scrubbing pass that removes expressions like {{...}} is skipped in DOM-return mode, and split text nodes (e.g. from removed intermediate tags) can rejoin to form a complete expression that template-evaluating frameworks like Vue 2 will execute."
          },
